    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="76.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 76.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.21"/> hit under þæs wifes cæglocan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.22"/> gebroht wære, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.23"/> heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ buton hit under ðæs wifes cæglocan gebroht wære, sy heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ buton hit under þes wifes cæglocum gebroht wære, syo heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Et nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.17"/> sub custodia uxoris suę positum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.18"/> sit, ipsa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.19"/> innocens habeatur.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Et nisi illud furtum inuentum fuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.14"/> sub clauibus mulieris, sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.15"/> illa immunis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>[76, 1] Et nisi sub seris marite locatum sit, immunis a crimine habeatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="76.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="212" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ buton hit under ðæs wifes cæglocan gebroht wære, sy heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And butan hit under þæs wifes cæglocan gebroht wære, si heo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn es nicht unter des Eheweibes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.de.1"/> Verschluss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.de.2"/> (Schlösser? <hi rend="italic">so A</hi>) gebracht worden ist<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-1.lnote.de.3"/>, stehe sie rein da.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And unless it was brought under the wife's lock (locks?, so A), let her stand clean.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="213" ed="#robertson"/>And unless the goods had been put under the wife's lock and key, she shall be clear [of any charge of complicity].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="473" ed="#whitelock"/>And unless it has been brought under the wife’s lock and key, she is to be clear.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="295" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And unless the goods had been placed under the wife’s lock and key, she shall be considered innocent.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="363"><ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd.</note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 363, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: added from Rabin p. 294, October 2026 (Rabin’s note to the text)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hordern: heddernes cæge B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">cyste: cyste cæge B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þonne: þone B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gelogian: gelaðyan A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si non <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si non Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ponatur <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ponatur Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so K</hi>; <hi rend="italic">fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus K; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sit <hi rend="italic">H Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sit H Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. i. i. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. i. i. lacking in Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ehefrau 9ff. Vielleicht ist Ine benutzt; <hi rend="italic">ebd</hi>. 9. Auf den Fortschritt in der Selbständigkeit des Weibes weist hin Roeder <hi rend="italic">Familie bei Agsa</hi>. 85; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 21</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ehefrau 9ff. Perhaps Ine has been used; <hi rend="italic">ibid</hi>. 9. The advance in the independence of woman is pointed out by Roeder <hi rend="italic">Familie bei Agsa</hi>. 85; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 21</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Schlüssel.—Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>. nimmt <hi rend="italic">cæglocan</hi> als Plural: ‘repositories . . with key’, was aber nur für A sicher ist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Schlüssel.—Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>. takes <hi rend="italic">cæglocan</hi> as a plural: ‘repositories . . with key’, which, however, is certain only for A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">76, 1. a in Inst-Version wird benutzt von Bracton III 32, 9, f. 151b. Nur diesem folgt das von Price als Benutzer angeführte Schott. Rechtsbuch 13 Jhs. <hi rend="italic">Quoniam attachiamenta</hi> XII 7, ed. <hi rend="italic">Acts of parliam. of Scotl</hi>. I 285</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">76, 1. a in the Inst version is used by Bracton III 32, 9, f. 151b. It is only Bracton that is followed by the Scottish law-book of the 13th cent. cited by Price as a borrower, <hi rend="italic">Quoniam attachiamenta</hi> XII 7, ed. <hi rend="italic">Acts of parliam. of Scotl</hi>. I 285</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_76-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. In. 7; 7, 1; 57.</seg></note>
      </div>
